# Thread C Collection Universe v1 artifacts are published WITH SHA-256 hashes
# (see research/THREADC_COLLECTION_UNIVERSE_V1.md section 4). Git's autocrlf
# would rewrite line endings on checkout on Windows and every one of those
# hashes would stop matching the file on disk. Pin these to LF so the bytes a
# reader hashes are the bytes that were hashed here.
research/THREADC_COLLECTION_UNIVERSE_V1.md   text eol=lf
research/threadc_universe_v1/*.json          text eol=lf
research/threadc_universe_v1/SHA256SUMS      text eol=lf
research/threadc_universe_v1/*.gz            binary

# systemd parses a unit file line by line; a CRLF checkout on Windows would put
# a stray \r at the end of every directive value and the unit would fail to load
# on the Linux host it is deployed to. Pin it to LF.
deploy/*.service                             text eol=lf
